# Copy to .env (git-ignored).
#
# ★ The one switch that decides whether this app has its own accounts or
#   shares the platform's. ★
#
#   SET    → sign-in, registration and Scan History go to CYPHIX_SERVER
#            (/api/v1). Same users table, same FHIR Patients, same
#            recordings as CYPHIX_MEDICAL_WEB: register in the browser,
#            sign in on the phone, same person. `useCurrentUser` also
#            switches to the REAL principal, so the client's RBAC matches
#            what the server will actually allow.
#   EMPTY  → fully offline: device-local mock accounts (AsyncStorage +
#            SHA-256 digests) and the on-device recording store. The demo
#            works on a plane; nothing leaves the phone.
#
# No trailing slash, and NO /api/v1 — the client appends it.
#
# Deployed:  https://cyphix-api.onrender.com   ← the normal choice. Not a
#            secret (it is a public endpoint), and the same database the web
#            app talks to. Free tier: sleeps after ~15 min idle, ~50 s to wake.
# Local dev: http://<this machine's LAN IP>:8080 — never `localhost`, which a
#            phone or emulator resolves to ITSELF. Find it with `ipconfig`
#            (the Wi-Fi adapter) and run `npm run dev` in ../CYPHIX_SERVER.
#            Only worth it when you are stepping through server code.
#
# ⚠️ EXPO_PUBLIC_* is inlined at BUNDLE time. After changing this, stop
#    `npm start` and start it again — reloading the app is not enough.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=
